# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DEVELOPER PORTAL - ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── REQUIRED FOR VERCEL PRODUCTION ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Add these environment variables in Vercel Project Settings → Environment Variables
#

# Backend API Base URL (REQUIRED)
# ✓ For Render Backend:
VITE_API_URL=https://sym-ecosystem-backend.onrender.com
#
# ✓ For Local Development:
# VITE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
#
# API Endpoints Called:
#   - Portal API (JWT auth):  /api/v1/dev-portal/*
#   - Public API (X-API-Key): /api/v1/developer/*
#

# ── OPTIONAL (if using client-side Neon database queries) ─────────────────
#
# Note: The developer portal doesn't directly use this, but included for future
# features or if you need to call your database from the frontend.
#
# VITE_NEON_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host/database?sslmode=require
#

# ── OPTIONAL (if Gemini features are exposed to frontend) ─────────────────
#
# Note: Usually this stays on the backend only for security.
# Only add here if frontend needs direct Gemini access.
#
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key
#

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CRITICAL SETUP CHECKLIST
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# ✓ Step 1: Add VITE_API_URL to Vercel
#   URL: https://sym-ecosystem-backend.onrender.com
#
# ✓ Step 2: Ensure Backend CORS is updated
#   Add to backend CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS:
#   - https://your-dev-portal.vercel.app  (your frontend URL)
#
# ✓ Step 3: Verify Backend is Running on Render
#   Check: https://sym-ecosystem-backend.onrender.com/api/v1/dev-portal/dashboard/
#   (Should return 401 Unauthorized, not connection error)
#
# ✓ Step 4: Redeploy Backend after updating CORS
#   Go to Render → Backend Service → Manual Deploy
#
# ✓ Step 5: Test Frontend
#   Visit: https://your-dev-portal.vercel.app
#   Try to login - should connect to backend
#
